==English==

===Etymology===
From {{der|en|frm|quartil}}, from {{der|en|ML.|quartilus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈkwɔː(ɹ)taɪl/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-quartile.wav |Audio (Southern England)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|statistics}} Any of the three [[point]]s that divide an [[ordered]] [[distribution]] into four parts, each containing a [[quarter]] of the [[population]].
# {{lb|en|statistics}} Any one of the four groups so divided.
#: {{ux|en|This school is ranked in the first '''quartile'''.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2021 July 28|author=Paul Clifton|title=Network News: Confusion and dissent over face mask requirements: Reaction to the Guidance: British Safety Council|journal=RAIL|issue=936|page=6|text=The Department for Transport's National Travel Survey shows that workers in the lowest income '''quartile''' are twice as likely to use public transport.}}

